Alright, let’s lay out the exact steps with commands so you can make your PostgreSQL PC act as the database server for all other PCs on your LAN. Since you’re developing on that same PC, you’ll use 127.0.0.1 locally, and other PCs will use your PC’s IPv4 address.

🖥️ On the PostgreSQL PC (the server)
Find your IPv4 address

Windows:

powershell
ipconfig
Look under your active network adapter → IPv4 Address (e.g., 192.168.1.10).

Linux/macOS:

bash
ip addr show
or

bash
ifconfig
Edit postgresql.conf

Location (Windows default): C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\<version>\data\postgresql.conf

Location (Linux): /etc/postgresql/<version>/main/postgresql.conf

Find the line:

conf
#listen_addresses = 'localhost'
Change it to:

conf
listen_addresses = '*'
Edit pg_hba.conf

Same folder as postgresql.conf.

Add a line to allow LAN connections:

Code
host    all    all    192.168.1.0/24    md5
Replace 192.168.1.0/24 with your LAN subnet. If unsure, use your PC’s IP with /32:

Code
host    all    all    192.168.1.10/32    md5
Restart PostgreSQL

Windows:

powershell
net stop postgresql-x64-14
net start postgresql-x64-14
(replace 14 with your version)

Linux:

bash
sudo systemctl restart postgresql
Create a database and user

sql
CREATE DATABASE payment_advice;
CREATE USER appuser WITH PASSWORD 'strongpassword';
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE payment_advice TO appuser;
Open firewall port 5432

Windows:

powershell
netsh advfirewall firewall add rule name="Postgres" dir=in action=allow protocol=TCP localport=5432
Linux (UFW):

bash
sudo ufw allow 5432/tcp
📂 In your Node.js/Electron project
Install pg

bash
npm install pg
Use environment variables

Create .env:

Code
DB_HOST=192.168.1.10
DB_PORT=5432
DB_USER=appuser
DB_PASS=strongpassword
DB_NAME=payment_advice
Load with dotenv:

js
require("dotenv").config();
const { Pool } = require("pg");

const pool = new Pool({
  host: process.env.DB_HOST,
  port: process.env.DB_PORT,
  user: process.env.DB_USER,
  password: process.env.DB_PASS,
  database: process.env.DB_NAME,
});
Local vs LAN

On your PC (dev): use DB_HOST=127.0.0.1.

On other PCs (clients): use DB_HOST=<your IPv4> (e.g., 192.168.1.10).

🚀 Deployment summary
Your PC runs PostgreSQL and acts as the server.

Other PCs only need your app .exe.

Your app connects to your PC’s IPv4 address (192.168.1.10) on port 5432.

PostgreSQL config + firewall must allow LAN connections.

